WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.200
Turn a newt's eye upside down, then cut the optic nerve and let it regrow.

2
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:13.860
Hold a lure above its head, and the newt turns its head down.

3
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.000
It kept making that mistake for as long as anyone watched.

4
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.260
Each regrown axon went back to the place it came from.

5
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.900
How does an axon know where to go?

6
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:31.110
The retina sends its axons to a target in the midbrain, the tectum.

7
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.110
The map is orderly.

8
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.210
Neighbours in the retina connect to neighbours in the tectum.

9
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:43.850
In the chick, axons from the temporal retina, the side nearer the temple, end in the

10
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:44.910
front of the tectum.

11
00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.790
Nasal axons end in the back.

12
00:00:48.683 --> 00:00:52.183
A growth cone is the moving tip of an axon.

13
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:57.303
It senses only what is close, yet the map spans the whole target.

14
00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:00.963
The answer is a pair of opposite slopes.

15
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:07.923
In the retina, the receptor EphA is high on the temporal side and low on the nasal

16
00:01:07.923 --> 00:01:13.943
side. In the tectum, the ligand ephrin-A rises from front to back.

17
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:20.833
Temporal axons carry the most EphA, so a little ephrin-A repels them.

18
00:01:21.313 --> 00:01:23.353
They stop in the front of the tectum.

19
00:01:24.453 --> 00:01:28.533
Nasal axons carry little EphA and tolerate more ephrin-A.

20
00:01:29.193 --> 00:01:30.933
They travel on into the back.

21
00:01:31.993 --> 00:01:37.773
One simple idea is that each axon stops where its own receptor meets enough ligand.

22
00:01:38.617 --> 00:01:44.337
An axon might read an absolute level of EphA, or compare itself with its neighbours.

23
00:01:45.337 --> 00:01:50.257
In mouse, researchers gave a random half of the retinal cells extra EphA.

24
00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:55.537
If axons read absolute levels, only those cells should shift forward.

25
00:01:56.497 --> 00:02:01.477
Instead, the cells with extra EphA took the front of the target, and their normal

26
00:02:01.477 --> 00:02:03.017
neighbours were pushed to the back.

27
00:02:03.997 --> 00:02:06.577
Two orderly maps filled the target together.

28
00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.547
So each axon is judged against the others.

29
00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:15.047
Its ending depends on its EphA signal relative to its neighbours.

30
00:02:16.147 --> 00:02:19.387
Axons compete for space, and the map is the outcome.

31
00:02:20.327 --> 00:02:23.067
Each growth cone senses only a short distance.

32
00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:29.187
Yet local rules give global order, because every axon is also sensing the others.
